<h2>Total Loss or Repair?</h2>
<p>After a tornado, insurers sometimes scope a home as repairable when the damage is more extensive than it looks. Racked walls, shifted framing, cracked slabs, and damaged roof decking can be hard to see once debris is cleared. In other cases the cost to repair approaches or exceeds the dwelling limit. An independent inspection, sometimes with an engineer, helps establish which applies. Matterport 3D imaging and thorough photos also preserve the condition of the property before demolition.</p>

